{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at exact 4f51610c992aafec797192fb67863ed87145a646 on request/scope-contract-r15, under promise git:sha1…3623eef on request git:sha1…3d81007\n\nScope and replay contract, revision 16 at 4f51610c992aafec797192fb67863ed87145a646 (one commit on adopted revision 15, 7f1ea903), for request a23dc307. All four subjects; the two companions are unchanged. EH9, the kind of an outcome entry: the outcome input gains owner and kind, set by the judge from the opening operation effect, and the entry's kind is owner:kind, as in hold@1:check. Deriving it from the entry's record was not taken: a refused or unknown outcome holds no record, two operations can write one record kind, and a foreign reader holds no table of the capability. Every outcome entry's bytes change; no deployed history holds one. A fact guard over such an entry checks kind and definition name; the kind says nothing of the result. One validator rule is added: no act kind or message name begins with platform:. EH10, contract side: every rule declares the most effects, requests and operations it returns; the validator counts them into the entry's bounds, with a new bound on the derived effects of one entry; a refusable entry past a bound is refused entry-too-large; for an entry that cannot be refused, the opening that would raise the state past its bound is refused instead. Numbers stay with the proof plan. EH2 and EH4 are accepted as built: workspace effects are a sixth effect group, after hold ends and before attention; a bound request refused unknown-message is still a settling entry with the one decided record. The four wording points of approval ac9b09f0 are applied. Source rows I3-12 to I3-16 are added. Read with the authority note's revision 21, filed with it. Reading limits: single writer; the validator, the bytes package and tests were not read. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"4f51610c992aafec797192fb67863ed87145a646","p